0116: let stage 11 run when stage 10 fails

The first level-11 boot printed stage 9 and stage 10 and then stopped.
Stage 10 treated "the root clock did not wake the block" as a dead end
and returned, so the stage-11 code sitting below it never executed - the
log had every line it should have had except the S11 ones, which is
exactly the failure mode that is easy to read past.

The two stages answer different halves of the same question: 10 asks
whether the clock root feeds the block, 11 whether the CX APB branch
does. Stage 11 has to run either way. The dead path now falls through,
and only the closing sequence (bus buffers, AO gating, reset release)
stays inside the alive branch, because that sequence is meaningless
against a window that drops writes.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
index af8c67e..c24e6db 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -1595,29 +1595,32 @@ sweet_gpu_probe(void)
         }
         printf("SWEET GPU: s10 alive=%d\n", cfg_up != 0);
         if (!cfg_up) {
+                /* Not a dead end: stage 11 asks the other half of the same
+                 * question, and returning here is exactly what swallowed it on
+                 * the first stage-11 boot. */
                 printf("SWEET GPU: s10 clock root did not wake the block\n");
-                return;
+        } else {
+                /* The block answers, so the vendor's pre-boot configuration
+                 * finally has something to land on: bus buffers, AO clock
+                 * gating, then the reset the CM3 has been held in. No firmware
+                 * is loaded, so the only outcome expected from the release is
+                 * the invalid-firmware code. */
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S10 wake CM3_SYSRESET=%#x HFI_VERSION_INFO=%#x AO=%#x\n",
+                    sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET),
+                    sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_HFI_VERSION_INFO),
+                    sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_STATUS));
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_SYS_BUS_CONFIG, 1u);
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CGC_MODE_CNTL, 0x20202u);
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S10 SYS_BUS_CONFIG=%#x CGC_MODE_CNTL=%#x\n",
+                    sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_SYS_BUS_CONFIG),
+                    sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CGC_MODE_CNTL));
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_PWR_COL_CP_RESP, 0u);
+                sweet_gpu_wr(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 0u);
+                delay(2000);
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S10 CM3_SYSRESET=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET));
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S10 CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT));
+                printf("SWEET GMU: S10 CM3_FW_BUSY=%#x\n", sweet_gpu_rd(gmu, SWEET_GMU_CM3_FW_BUSY));
         }
